{
    "background_story": "Mariam was a free-spirited artist who lived life on her own terms. She had a 'bucket list' that was as colorful as her paintings. From skydiving over the Great Barrier Reef to learning the art of traditional African drumming, Mariam was determined to experience it all. But one item on her list stood out - to create a massive mural using nothing but buckets of paint and a few trusty brushes. Mariam spent weeks preparing for the project, gathering buckets of every shape and size. Finally, the day arrived, and she set to work on the city's largest wall, transforming it into a vibrant masterpiece. As she dipped her brush into the last bucket of paint, Mariam felt an overwhelming sense of fulfillment, knowing she had truly made her mark on the world.",
